* linguist-language=cpp

# Evidence pipeline: bytes that are hashed must not be transformed by git (ADR-007).
#
# Every recipe, every source asset a recipe names, and every artifact baked from them has its
# SHA-256 recorded and byte-compared across MSVC, GCC and Clang. GitHub's Windows runners default
# to core.autocrlf=true, so without these rules a `.toml` recipe would be checked out with CRLF on
# Windows and LF everywhere else - a different digest, and an `evidence.*` test that fails on the
# MSVC leg alone while every other leg stays green.
#
# `-text` means "store and check out verbatim": no end-of-line conversion in either direction.
recipes/** -text
generated/** -text

# A test fixture that is byte-compared needs the same rule for the same reason. `medui-package-*`
# and `medui-screen-emit-fixture-is-current` compare a committed package.json against what the
# compiler produces in memory, so a checkout that added carriage returns would fail on the MSVC leg
# alone - which is exactly how this was found.
tests/medui/fixtures/** -text

# The published `.medui` contract is emitted as canonical JSON - LF line endings, by definition -
# and `medui-grammar-committed-copy-is-current` compares the committed file against what the
# compiler emits, byte for byte. Same rule for the same reason, and found the same way: the MSVC leg
# alone reported 24041 bytes committed against 23235 emitted, which is one carriage return per line.
docs/medui/** -text

# The generated tool manifest is compared byte for byte by `generate_tool_manifest.py --check`, so
# it needs the rule for the same reason `docs/medui/` does. Added with the file rather than after the
# MSVC leg found it, which is how the two entries above this one were arrived at.
docs/tools/** -text

# Rendered-truth fixtures are also parsed and byte-compared as canonical JSON. Keep their bytes
# identical when Windows checks them out, including fixtures that deliberately contain no golden.
tests/verify_ui/fixtures/** -text

# Unified-diff context lines that represent blank source lines contain the mandatory context
# prefix, which is trailing whitespace from the outer repository's perspective.
*.patch -whitespace
